---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/seo/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import PrivacyChoices from "../components/seo/PrivacyChoices.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../config/site";
const lastUpdated = "2026-11-09";
---

<Layout title="Privacy policy" description="How TimeAtlas handles local preferences, Google Analytics, Google AdSense cookies, and hosting logs.">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Privacy policy", href: "/privacy/" }]} />
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-paper-100">Privacy policy</h1>

    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-paper-600">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-paper-100">What TimeAtlas stores, and where</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-paper-300">
        TimeAtlas has no user accounts and no server-side database. Your preferences — saved
        comparison cities, your 12-hour/24-hour choice, and whether
        the globe auto-rotates — are saved only in your own browser's local storage, on your
        own device. We never see this data, it is never sent to any server, and it never
        leaves your device unless you clear your browser data yourself. If local storage is
        unavailable or full, TimeAtlas simply doesn't save your preferences for next time;
        nothing is lost beyond that.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-paper-300">
        None of this data is sensitive in nature (it's clock settings and city names), and
        TimeAtlas does not ask for, or store, anything that would be.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-paper-100">Cookies, advertising, and analytics</h2>
      {
        siteConfig.googleAnalyticsId && (
          <p class="mt-2 text-paper-300">
            Pages load Google Analytics to count visits, pages viewed, and general location and
            device information. Google Analytics sets cookies for that measurement. Google
            describes this in{" "}
            <a
              href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
              class="underline hover:text-paper-100"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              target="_blank">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services</a
            >.
          </p>
        )
      }
      {
        siteConfig.adsenseClientId ? (
          <>
            <p class="mt-2 text-paper-300">
              Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on earlier
              visits to this site or other sites. Google's advertising cookies help Google and its
              partners select ads based on those visits. TimeAtlas does not use another advertising
              vendor. The only advertising script this build loads is Google AdSense.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-paper-300">
              You can control ad personalization, including turning personalized ads off, at{" "}
              <a
                href="https://myadcenter.google.com/"
                class="underline hover:text-paper-100"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                target="_blank">Google's My Ad Center</a
              >. Google also describes this in{" "}
              <a
                href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads"
                class="underline hover:text-paper-100"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                target="_blank">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services</a
              >.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-paper-300">
              Visitors in the EEA, UK, and Switzerland should also get Google's European regulations
              message when that message is published in AdSense. Use the button below to reopen those
              choices. If the consent script is not available, the button says so instead of doing nothing.
            </p>
            <PrivacyChoices />
          </>
        ) : (
          !siteConfig.googleAnalyticsId && (
            <p class="mt-2 text-paper-300">
              This build does not load an advertising or analytics script, and TimeAtlas does not
              set its own tracking cookies. Saved clock preferences stay in your browser's local
              storage.
            </p>
          )
        )
      }
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-paper-100">Hosting logs</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-paper-300">
        Like virtually all web hosting, the infrastructure serving this site will typically
        keep ordinary request logs (such as IP address, requested URL, and timestamp) for
        operational and security purposes, for a limited retention period, as is standard
        practice for static web hosting. The specifics depend on {siteConfig.operatorName || "the operator's"}{" "}
        chosen hosting provider and should be confirmed and detailed here before a public
        launch.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-paper-100">Third-party data requests</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-paper-300">
        Fonts are loaded from Google Fonts over HTTPS, which involves your browser making a
        request to Google's servers for that font file, subject to Google's own privacy
        practices.
        {
          siteConfig.googleAnalyticsId &&
            " When analytics is enabled, the page also requests Google Analytics."
        }
        {
          siteConfig.adsenseClientId &&
            " When advertising is enabled, the page also requests Google's AdSense script."
        }
        {
          !siteConfig.googleAnalyticsId &&
            !siteConfig.adsenseClientId &&
            " The clocks, search, and globe themselves do not call another third-party service."
        }
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-paper-100">Questions</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-paper-300">
        The publisher is named on the <a href="/contact/" class="underline hover:text-paper-100">contact page</a>.
        {
          siteConfig.contactEmail && (
            <>
              {" "}Email{" "}
              <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`} class="underline hover:text-paper-100">{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>
              {" "}with questions about this page.
            </>
          )
        }
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
